  <layout>One column of running text, with marginal notes in the right margin. Running head centred at the top, printed page number at top right. The text is cut off at the foot of the scan, so the page is transcribed up to the last visible line.</layout>
  <page_number>89</page_number>
  <running_head>De Duellis.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <p cont="true">quodque reipublicæ membrum pro aris & socis stare tenetur, & bona, parentes, liberos, conjugem, patriam tueri, ejusque securitatem redemptam cupere, etiam cum sui ipsius internecione. <note side="right">Init.in-ftir. Ex-cuf. Fu-tor.</note>Hoc ipsum passim collaudat jus civile. Quienim pro patria moritur, in perpetuum per gloriam vivere creditur. Qui fu-pervivit, honoribus ac præmiis, quæ meritus est afficiendus. <note side="right">l.35. D. de Relig. gloss. &amp; sumpt. Gloss. in l. velut. 2. D. de iustit. &amp;</note>Quinimo non tantum licitum, aut liberè relictum, pro <illegible, ~20 letters></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The first note's and second note's wording in the right margin is partly abbreviated and cut; "giof." in the second note is read as "gloss." with doubt, and the last margin line is cut off. The last text line is only partly visible.</notes>
</page>
<page type="text">
  <layout>One column of running text, with marginal notes in the right margin. Below the last line, at the right, a catchword.</layout>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Nec</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p cont="true">patria sic decertare, sed etiam si occasio suadeat, omnino necessarium censebitur.</p>
    <p>Quo nomine historiis proditum exemplum mulierisLacenæ, quæ cum accepisset[?] filium ignavo erga patriam fuisse animo, domum reversum occidit, ejusque sepulchro hosce versus inscribi curavit: <i>Hunc timidum mater Damatrion</i> <note side="right"><i>Iustin.&amp;</i> jur. &amp; in l. fallaciter. Cod. de Abolit.</note><i>ipsa peremit.</i> <note side="right">Valer. Max. libr. 2. cap. 7.</note>Nec</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The first line of the right margin note is cut at the top of the scan; the reading "Iustin.&amp;" is a likely reading. "accepisset" is partly overlapped by the next word in the print and is uncertain. The word "Nec" at the foot is the catchword. The paragraph opening at the top continues from the previous page.</notes>
</page>